## (4) thermal LinearSolveFailure seen in (3b) at 'smooth0.08 tol1e-06 0.8/0.4' (NOT conv, 27 it): replay of the production
## Picard loop (ThermalSolver settings: BiCGSTAB abs 1e-12 / rel 1e-10 / 1000, outer tol 1e-8) on the same flow field.
## Outer 27: BiCGSTAB Breakdown at residual 9.649e-12 (from 2.505e-8), above both the absolute tolerance 1e-12 and
## rel * r_ref = 6.314e-12, so runPicardLoop reports LinearSolveFailure; a loop that continued would converge at outer 29.
## Cause: BiCGSTAB's breakdown tests compare scale-dependent inner products with the absolute constants::tiny = 1e-30
## (src/algebra/BiCGSTAB.cpp); near round-off (residual ~1e-11) the shadow-residual product (rHat, r) can fall below it.
## This is a pre-existing thermal/linear-solver robustness limitation, not a mesh-quality defect; it is recorded as a
## limitation (summary.md section 21) and NOT changed in P12-MESH-004 (no solver-behaviour change). The campaign settings
## (acceptance_gate.md) are SIMPLE tolerance 1e-7, relaxation 0.8/0.4, at which the same case converged in (3b).
# linear settings abs 1e-12 rel 1e-10 max 1000; outer tol 1e-08
